Purpose: Make Bash the only shell (Plan 0003, Locked Decision 3). The core shell module keeps only its Bash registry entry: resolution returns Bash for every request (a requested name is honored only when it names a Bash executable), the Windows candidate chain, the Git Bash lookup, the macOS default, and the per-shell argument builders for fish, zsh, dash, ksh, sh, nu, cmd, PowerShell, and pwsh are deleted, as is the taskkill branch of killTree. The shell tool loses its PowerShell machinery (the tree-sitter PowerShell parser, the ps scan path, cygpath translation, and the cmd/PowerShell prompt sections and shell kinds), the core bash tool resolves its default shell through the shell module, and the PTY loses its Windows environment block. The two shell test files are updated to assert the Bash-only contract, including removal of the tests for the deleted Git Bash surface.
Upstream files: packages/core/src/shell.ts, packages/core/src/tool/bash.ts, packages/core/src/pty.ts, packages/opencode/src/tool/shell.ts, packages/opencode/src/tool/shell/id.ts, packages/opencode/src/tool/shell/prompt.ts, packages/core/test/shell.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/tool/shell.test.ts
Rebase note: Check the shell module's export surface first (preferred, acceptable, args, list, name, login, posix, killTree); callers across the tree depend on exactly those names. The prompt file is regenerated from the shell.txt template placeholders, which are unchanged.

